<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odano Naotake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1749–1780</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Odano Naotake was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> painter of the Kubota domain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akita">Akita</a> and the leading artist of the Akita school, which combined Japanese subjects with Western perspective and shading. Taught by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiraga-gennai">Hiraga Gennai</a> from 1773, he went to Edo and drew the illustrations for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaitai-shinsho">Kaitai Shinsho</a> (1774), the first Japanese translation of a European anatomy text. He died young in 1780.</p></div>
